==English==
{{was wotd|2024|August|21}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|h₂éd}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱer-|id=grow}}
{{lbor|en|la|accrētiō|t=increase, increment}} + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ion|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|noun}}s denoting actions or processes, or their results}}. {{m|la||Accrētiō}} is derived from {{m|la|accrēscō|t=to grow; to increase}} + {{m|la|-tiō|pos=suffix forming nouns denoting actions or processes, or their results}};<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=1129480294|date=December 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> and {{m|la||accrēscō}} is from {{m|la|ac-}} (a variant of {{m|la|ad-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘to’, or having an {{glossary|intensifying}} effect}}) + {{m|la|crēscō|t=to grow; to increase}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱer-|t=to cause to grow; to grow; to nourish}}). {{doublet|en|accrue|crescent|increase}}.

